cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "VeriSec Forge: Relation-Preserving Secure Patch Reasoning"
version: "0.1.0"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "VeriSec Forge contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cyb2oo2/verisec-forge"
url: "https://github.com/cyb2oo2/verisec-forge"
abstract: >
  VeriSec Forge is a research artifact for studying relation-preserving
  behavior in secure patch reasoning. It includes VeriPatch-RR relational
  benchmark artifacts, retained smoke and audit reports, decoder controls,
  and external-adapter reproducibility paths. It is not a deployed
  vulnerability scanner, leaderboard, or generic model-quality benchmark.
keywords:
  - secure patch reasoning
  - relational evaluation
  - vulnerability detection
  - paired-diff evaluation
  - research artifact
license: Apache-2.0
